      "claim_id": "majority-ground",
      "proposition": "The Court will hold that under 28 U.S.C. \u00a7 2244(b)(2)(A), the phrase 'previously unavailable' modifies 'a new rule of constitutional law,' meaning that a rule is available as soon as it is announced by the Supreme Court, regardless of whether a petitioner's specific claim had a possibility of success under the clinical or evidentiary standards existing at the time of a prior petition."
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "ground-breadth",
      "proposition": "The Court will establish a categorical rule that a new rule of constitutional law is 'available' for purposes of AEDPA's successive-petition bar immediately upon its announcement by the Supreme Court, strictly foreclosing any futility exception or case-specific inquiry into the practical viability of the claim during prior habeas proceedings."
    }
  ],
